police in the Bahamas say seven  Americans were killed in a helicopter  crash on July 4th the aircraft went down  about two miles from Grand Cay Island  killing everyone on board  they include billionaire coal tycoon and  philanthropist Chris Klein CTM lead  national correspondent David Begg know  is here with the very latest  Jericka good morning there were four  females and two other males on board now  Bahamian police have not yet told us the  identities of the victims the bodies we  understand have all been retrieved from  the ocean water they've been taken to  Grand Bahamas police and civilian  aviation authorities including those  from the u.s. investigate what went  wrong shortly after taking off from  Grand Cay Island this helicopter crashed  into the Atlantic Ocean it was heading  from one of the Bahamas northernmost  islands to Fort Lauderdale Florida on  the 4th of July authorities found the  helicopters submerged in 16 feet of  water after learning it did not arrive  at its destination former NTSB chairman  Mark Rosen Kirk says US officials will  work with Bahamian authorities to  determine what happened self-made  billionaire Chris Klein is among the  victims one of his daughters was  reportedly on the plane with him Klein  was a well-known philanthropist in his  native West Virginia  according to Forbes he joined the family  coal business at a young age and began  working in underground mines at just 15  years old he later developed some of the  most productive and economical coal  mines in the United States  Bloomberg called him the new king coal  on Thursday night West Virginia's  governor Jim Justice said on Twitter  that he lost a very close friend and  that Klein was always there to give what  a wonderful loving and giving man today  would have been Chris Klein's  62nd birthday you know something  interesting about the crash the chopper  took off around 2:00 a.m. but it wasn't  reported missing until police we're told  about it around 12 hours later  that's when it didn't show up in Fort  Lauderdale very horrifying just a little  detail about today would have been his  birthday that's that that always makes  it even worse to me when you hear that  they died actually on their birthday and  that no day's a good day to die but  that's always time that he was with his  daughter and we still don't know the  identities of the others all right David  thank you very much we'll see you again  tonight on the CBS Evening News
 

